rve from the thermocouple attached to the sample (Fig. 3b). The MS values obtained by DleT and Tet curves were consistent with each other within an experimental uncertainty of 20 K.","second_reader_agrees":true,"stated_uncertainty":"20 K","type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":true,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-7I6YGM3K2O","nominal_composition":"Tiex at%Vey at%Al(ez at% Fe)","page":2,"purity":"99.98%Ti, 99.7%V, 99.999%Al, 99.7%Fe","quote":"Experimental TieVeAl and TieVeAleFe alloys, denoted as \"Cxey(ez)\" or \"Dxey(ez)\" roughly for Tiex at%Vey at%Al(ez at% Fe), were prepared by arc-melting using pure elements (99.98%Ti, 99.7%V, 99.999%Al, 99.7%Fe).","second_reader_agrees":true,"starting_materials":"pure elements (99.98%Ti, 99.7%V, 99.999%Al, 99.7%Fe)","synthesis":"arc-melting","type":"sample"},{"applies_to":"some buttons","cooling":"quenching in iced brine","duration":"1 h","duration_parsed":{"hours":1.0,"printed":"1 h"},"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-N64ZFWE4TB","page":2,"purpose":"recrystallized","quote":"For the convenience of machining, some buttons were cold rolled and recrystallized at 1073 K for 1 h followed by quenching in iced brine.","second_reader_agrees":true,"temperature":{"T_K":1073.0,"converted_in_code":false,"printed":"1073 K","unit_basis":"printed_with_value","unit_printed":"K","value_printed":1073.0},"temperature_printed":"1073 K","temperature_status":"parsed_from_printed","type":"treatment"}],"paper":"doi:10.1016/j.jallcom.2016.02.251","reader_tier":"preliminary_flash","readers":["gemini-3.8-flash / exp-context-v2.1-quote","claude-opus-5.5 / exp-context-v2.1-quote (claude broker)"],"section_basis":"methods_heading"}},"elements":["AL","FE","TI","V"],"licence":"CC BY 4.0 (derived data; quotes under fair use)","models":{},"note":"records[].locator.ref -> artifacts; records[].model -> models (full records: orchid-literature.jsonl.gz)","papers":{"doi:10.1016/j.jallcom.2016.02.251":{"authors":["Jia-Yi Yan","G.B. Olson"],"citation":"J